      'A honeymoon photoshoot in Porto gives you what the wedding album cannot: the pair of you in your own clothes, a few days after the big day, with nothing left to organise. The city suits that mood. It is made for slow walks, long dinners and late nights, and thirty minutes with a photographer slips into that without taking it over. Wedding pictures record an event; these record a couple on holiday, unhurried, somewhere you chose together, and plenty of people come to prefer them.',
    where:
      'Two settings fit a honeymoon particularly well, and the booking takes one. Foz do Douro at sundown is the classic: the river runs into the Atlantic, nothing blocks the horizon, and the wind and space make every frame feel loose. São Bento at seven in the morning is the surprise: a great hall lined with blue-and-white tiles, nearly deserted at that hour, with trains waiting behind you. Because it is a working station the window is short, but ten quiet minutes there can produce the most distinctive photographs of the whole trip.',
    when:
      'For Foz, arrive about an hour before the sun touches the water, which shifts from late evening in June to mid-afternoon in December. For São Bento, the hour around seven, before the commuter flow begins at eight. September and October make particularly good honeymoon months here, warm but uncrowded, and the Douro harvest is a day trip away for anyone with a spare day.',
